---
import ContentLayout from '@/layouts/content-layout.astro'
import {
	CTO_TIERS,
	ENGAGEMENT_TERMS,
	FULL_TIME_CTO_SALARY,
	MVP_BUILD_FROM,
	STRATEGY_SESSION,
	effectiveHourlyRate,
	formatUsd,
} from '@/lib/pricing'

const cheapest = CTO_TIERS[0]
const priciest = CTO_TIERS[CTO_TIERS.length - 1]
const fractional = CTO_TIERS.find((t) => t.id === 'fractional')!
const hourlyRates = CTO_TIERS.map(effectiveHourlyRate)
const minHourly = Math.min(...hourlyRates)
const maxHourly = Math.max(...hourlyRates)
const monthlySalary = Math.round(FULL_TIME_CTO_SALARY / 12)
const salaryShare = Math.round((fractional.monthlyPrice / monthlySalary) * 100)

const description = `Fractional CTO pricing from ${formatUsd(cheapest.monthlyPrice)} a month, or ${formatUsd(minHourly)} to ${formatUsd(maxHourly)} per hour. See what each plan includes and how it compares to a ${formatUsd(FULL_TIME_CTO_SALARY / 1000)}k full-time CTO hire.`
---

<ContentLayout title="Fractional CTO Cost and Rates (2026 Pricing) | Ilzam" description={description}>
	<div class="flex items-center gap-3">
		<span class="rounded-sm bg-muted px-2 py-0.5 text-xs font-medium uppercase">Pricing</span>
		<span class="text-xs text-muted-foreground">Updated October 2026</span>
	</div>

	<h1 class="mt-4 text-3xl font-light leading-tight tracking-tight md:text-4xl">
		Fractional CTO Cost and Rates
	</h1>

	<p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-relaxed">
		My fractional CTO plans cost {formatUsd(cheapest.monthlyPrice)} to {formatUsd(priciest.monthlyPrice)} per
		month, depending on how many hours you need. That works out to {formatUsd(minHourly)} to
		{formatUsd(maxHourly)} per hour. If you only need one decision made well, a single
		{STRATEGY_SESSION.minutes}-minute strategy session is {formatUsd(STRATEGY_SESSION.price)}.
	</p>
	<p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">{ENGAGEMENT_TERMS}</p>
	<p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
		New to the term? A fractional CTO is a part-time technology leader: the person who makes
		your technical decisions and keeps your developers on track, without the cost of a
		full-time executive.
	</p>

	<!-- Monthly plans -->
	<section class="mt-10">
		<h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Monthly plans</h2>
		<div class="mt-6 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-3">
			{
				CTO_TIERS.map((tier) => (
					<div class="flex flex-col rounded-lg border p-5">
						<p class="font-medium">{tier.name}</p>
						<p class="mt-3 text-3xl font-light tracking-tight">
							{formatUsd(tier.monthlyPrice)}
							<span class="text-sm text-muted-foreground"> / month</span>
						</p>
						<p class="mt-1 text-xs text-muted-foreground">
							About {tier.hoursPerMonth} hours, {formatUsd(effectiveHourlyRate(tier))}/hour
						</p>
						<p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed">{tier.summary}</p>
						<ul class="mt-4 flex-1 space-y-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground">
							{tier.includes.map((item) => (
								<li class="flex gap-2">
									<span class="mt-2 size-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-foreground" />
									{item}
								</li>
							))}
						</ul>
						<p class="mt-4 text-xs italic text-muted-foreground">Best for: {tier.bestFor}</p>
					</div>
				))
			}
		</div>

		<div class="mt-4 rounded-lg bg-muted/50 p-5">
			<p class="font-medium">
				Not ready for a monthly plan? {STRATEGY_SESSION.name}, {formatUsd(STRATEGY_SESSION.price)} one-off
			</p>
			<ul class="mt-3 space-y-1 text-sm text-muted-foreground">
				{STRATEGY_SESSION.includes.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}
			</ul>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- Hourly rate -->
	<section class="mt-12">
		<h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Fractional CTO hourly rate</h2>
		<p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
			I price by the month, not by the hour, so you can message me when something comes up
			without watching a meter. Here is what each plan works out to per hour.
		</p>
		<div class="mt-6 overflow-x-auto">
			<table class="w-full text-left text-sm">
				<thead>
					<tr class="border-b">
						<th class="py-3 pr-4 font-medium">Plan</th>
						<th class="py-3 pr-4 font-medium">Per month</th>
						<th class="py-3 pr-4 font-medium">Hours</th>
						<th class="py-3 font-medium">Per hour</th>
					</tr>
				</thead>
				<tbody class="text-muted-foreground">
					{
						CTO_TIERS.map((tier) => (
							<tr class="border-b">
								<td class="py-3 pr-4 text-foreground">{tier.name}</td>
								<td class="py-3 pr-4">{formatUsd(tier.monthlyPrice)}</td>
								<td class="py-3 pr-4">~{tier.hoursPerMonth}</td>
								<td class="py-3">{formatUsd(effectiveHourlyRate(tier))}</td>
							</tr>
						))
					}
				</tbody>
			</table>
		</div>
		<p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
			Smaller plans cost more per hour because every new client takes some fixed time to learn:
			your product, your existing code, and your team. I need that context before my advice is
			worth anything.
		</p>
	</section>

	<!-- Savings -->
	<section class="mt-12">
		<h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Does a fractional CTO actually save money?</h2>
		<p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
			A full-time CTO is a {formatUsd(FULL_TIME_CTO_SALARY)}+ salary commitment. That is about
			{formatUsd(monthlySalary)} a month before equity, benefits, and recruiting. The
			{fractional.name} plan is {formatUsd(fractional.monthlyPrice)} a month, roughly {salaryShare}% of
			the salary alone, and you can stop it with 2 weeks' notice instead of running a hiring and
			firing process.
		</p>
		<p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
			It stops saving money when you need a technical leader most of the week for months on end.
			At that point the {priciest.name} plan costs {formatUsd(priciest.monthlyPrice * 12)} a year, and a
			full-time hire who owns the role long term is often the better investment. I'll tell you when
			you've reached that point, and I can help you hire that person.
		</p>
	</section>

	<!-- Cost drivers -->
	<section class="mt-12">
		<h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">What changes the cost</h2>
		<div class="mt-6 space-y-4">
			<div class="rounded-lg bg-muted/50 p-5">
				<p class="font-medium">How much of my time you need</p>
				<p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
					This matters most, which is why the plans are sized by hours. A bigger plan means
					I'm more involved in planning the work, checking it, and hiring.
				</p>
			</div>
			<div class="rounded-lg bg-muted/50 p-5">
				<p class="font-medium">Whether I'm advising or building</p>
				<p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
					The Advisor and Fractional CTO plans cover advice, decisions, and leading your
					developers. If you also want me to build the product myself, that's the
					{priciest.name} plan, or a one-time build of your first version (an MVP) starting from
					{formatUsd(MVP_BUILD_FROM)}. To see what your product would cost to build, try the
					<a href="/tool/mvp-cost-estimator" class="underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-foreground">app and software development cost calculator</a>.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- CTA -->
	<section class="mt-12 rounded-lg border p-6">
		<h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Not sure which plan fits?</h2>
		<p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
			Book a free 30-minute intro call. No pitch, no pressure, just a real conversation about what
			you're building.
		</p>
		<a
			href="https://cal.com/ilzam/intro"
			target="_blank"
			rel="noopener noreferrer"
			class="mt-4 inline-flex rounded-full bg-foreground px-5 py-2 text-sm font-medium text-background transition-opacity hover:opacity-90"
		>
			Book a free intro call
		</a>
	</section>
</ContentLayout>
